---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SEOHead from '../components/SEOHead.astro';
import FocusObject from '../components/FocusObject.astro';
import { url } from '../utils/paths';
---
<Base
  title="The Lens. Your AI marketing team"
  description="The Lens turns senior marketing practice into 28 skills for Claude Cowork that read your brand context and ship the work alongside you."
>
  <SEOHead
    slot="seo"
    type="website"
    title="The Lens. Your AI marketing team"
    description="The Lens turns senior marketing practice into 28 skills for Claude Cowork that read your brand context and ship the work alongside you."
    breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'The Lens', url: '/lens' }]}
  />

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="section lens-hero dwell-pin">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={420} tiltX={62} tiltY={-18} spin={140} scrollSpin={-80} style="top: 4%; right: -6%;" enterFrom="right" />
      <FocusObject size={260} tiltX={55} tiltY={20} spin={-110} scrollSpin={90} style="bottom: -8%; left: -10%;" enterFrom="left" />

      <div class="container lens-hero-inner">
        <div class="eyebrow reveal">000 · THE LENS</div>
        <h1 class="lens-headline reveal">
          Meet your AI<br/>
          <span class="gradient-text">marketing team</span>.
        </h1>
        <p class="lens-lead reveal">
          We've distilled senior marketing operators into 28 skills for Claude
          Cowork that read your brand context and ship the work alongside you.
          There are 47 playbooks behind them. It's free to read and free to
          install. We refresh it as the models change.
        </p>
        <div class="lens-ctas reveal">
          <a href={url('/lens/start-here')} class="btn-cta">Start here</a>
          <a href={url('/lens/library')} class="btn-ghost">Browse the library</a>
        </div>
        <p class="lens-secondary-links reveal">
          If you need a refresher, read <a href={url('/lens/primer')}>The Lens 101</a> or the <a href={url('/lens/cowork')}>Cowork setup primer</a>. You can also measure where you stand with the <a href={url('/lens/ftp-test')}>Marketing FTP Test</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="lens-meta mono reveal">FREE · 47 playbooks · 28 skills · Endurance focus · Updated as the models shift</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE GAP -->
  <section class="section section-alt dwell-pin">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={320} tiltX={60} tiltY={-22} spin={150} scrollSpin={-70} style="top: 8%; left: 4%;" enterFrom="left" />
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">001 · THE GAP</div>
        <h2 class="big-statement reveal" data-scroll-scale style="transform-origin: left center;">
          Most senior marketers<br/>
          are using AI <span class="gradient-text">like a typewriter</span>.
        </h2>
        <div class="lens-grid">
          <p class="reveal">
            They draft a meta description in ChatGPT. They Midjourney a
            stock-photo replacement. They sit through webinars about agents,
            then walk away with a list of tools they'll never wire up. The
            pipeline still looks like 2020 with a faster pen.
          </p>
          <p class="reveal">
            The operators a step ahead use AI as a team. Their briefs iterate
            on themselves. Their pipelines improve every time a new model ships.
            They got there by seeing the workflow written down with every
            failure mode labelled.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT IT IS -->
  <section class="section dwell-pin">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={360} tiltX={58} tiltY={18} spin={-130} scrollSpin={100} style="top: 6%; right: 4%;" enterFrom="right" />
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">002 · WHAT IT IS</div>
        <h2 class="reveal">It's a living library you keep coming back to.</h2>
        <p class="lead reveal">
          The Lens is a curated reference for senior marketers. Each entry is
          a complete AI workflow, walked through end to end on a worked
          example. It gives you the prompts and the eval gates. It names the
          failure modes too.
        </p>

        <div class="lens-pillars stagger">
          <article class="lens-pillar">
            <div class="pillar-num mono">/A</div>
            <h3>You can run every playbook today</h3>
            <p>
              Each playbook is a step-by-step workflow with click-paths
              through the tools you already use. You get copy-paste prompts
              and downloadable templates. A worked example takes you through
              it end to end.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="lens-pillar">
            <div class="pillar-num mono">/B</div>
            <h3>Each one names its eval gates and failure modes</h3>
            <p>
              The prompts are the easy part. Each entry also gives you the
              quality checks the output should pass before it goes live. It
              lists the common ways the workflow breaks, with the signs that
              tell you which is happening. When you swap the model, you re-run
              the checks and ship.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="lens-pillar">
            <div class="pillar-num mono">/C</div>
            <h3>We refresh it as the models change</h3>
            <p>
              When a frontier model lands, we re-test the affected
              workflows and update the entries. If a model change breaks a
              workflow, we note in the entry what changed and what the new
              shape looks like, so the library stays current.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="lens-pillar">
            <div class="pillar-num mono">/D</div>
            <h3>You search first and browse second</h3>
            <p>
              Search by keyword, then filter by stack or brand stage. You
              pull the playbook you need for the brief on your desk this
              week.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PICK YOUR STARTING POINT -->
  <section class="section lens-first-time" id="diagnostic">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">003 · PICK YOUR STARTING POINT</div>
      <h2 class="reveal lens-first-headline">Answer two questions and get your starter playbook in twenty seconds.</h2>
      <p class="lens-first-lead reveal">
        The Lens has 47 playbooks, but you only need the right one for
        the work in front of you. The diagnostic finds it from your two
        answers.
      </p>

      <div class="lens-diagnostic reveal" data-diagnostic>
        <div class="diag-step" data-diag-step="1">
          <p class="diag-q">What's the work in front of you this week?</p>
          <div class="diag-options" data-diag-options="1"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="diag-step" data-diag-step="2" hidden>
          <p class="diag-q" data-diag-q2></p>
          <div class="diag-options" data-diag-options="2"></div>
          <button type="button" class="diag-back mono" data-diag-back>← BACK</button>
        </div>
        <div class="diag-step diag-result" data-diag-step="3" hidden>
          <div class="diag-result-tag mono">YOUR STARTER</div>
          <h3 class="diag-result-title" data-diag-title></h3>
          <p class="diag-result-why" data-diag-why></p>
          <p class="diag-result-meta mono" data-diag-meta></p>
          <div class="diag-result-ctas">
            <a href="#" class="btn-cta" data-diag-link>Open the playbook</a>
            <button type="button" class="btn-ghost" data-diag-restart>Start again</button>
          </div>
          <p class="diag-result-nudge">
            If you'd rather the agent ran it, <a href="#plugin">install the plugin</a> and ask Claude to set up The Lens.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="lens-first-tease reveal">
        For the fuller picture before you pick, take the <a href={url('/lens/ftp-test')}>Marketing FTP Test</a>. In two minutes you get a score across six dimensions, plus a training plan for your weakest one.
      </p>

      <p class="lens-first-divider mono reveal">OR BROWSE THE COMMON STARTING POINTS</p>

      <div class="lens-first-grid stagger">
        <a href={url('/lens/brand/positioning-audit-pipeline')} class="first-card">
          <div class="first-card-tag mono">START WITH</div>
          <h3>I've inherited a brand and need an honest read</h3>
          <p>Run a positioning audit and voice extraction, then build a message house. It takes about four working days.</p>
          <span class="first-card-cue mono">POSITIONING AUDIT →</span>
        </a>
        <a href={url('/lens/content/eval-gated-drafting')} class="first-card">
          <div class="first-card-tag mono">START WITH</div>
          <h3>I need to ship more content without losing the brand</h3>
          <p>Every draft passes voice and fact gates before a human sees it. Drafts that pass feed a social factory.</p>
          <span class="first-card-cue mono">EVAL-GATED DRAFTING →</span>
        </a>
        <a href={url('/lens/ops/brief-to-ship-pipeline')} class="first-card">
          <div class="first-card-tag mono">START WITH</div>
          <h3>The team ships but the system around it is chaos</h3>
          <p>Set up a brief-to-ship pipeline with structured intake and weekly triage. It replaces ten separate tools.</p>
          <span class="first-card-cue mono">BRIEF-TO-SHIP →</span>
        </a>
        <a href={url('/lens/demand/channel-mix-simulator')} class="first-card">
          <div class="first-card-tag mono">START WITH</div>
          <h3>I need to defend a budget allocation to the CFO</h3>
          <p>Use the channel-mix simulator with reach-curve fitting to walk into the meeting with three scenarios and the maths.</p>
          <span class="first-card-cue mono">CHANNEL-MIX SIMULATOR →</span>
        </a>
        <a href={url('/lens/productivity/daily-briefing-pipeline')} class="first-card">
          <div class="first-card-tag mono">START WITH</div>
          <h3>My day is reactive and I want it back</h3>
          <p>Pull your calendar and inbox into one five-minute morning brief. Slack and your CRM can feed it too.</p>
          <span class="first-card-cue mono">DAILY BRIEFING →</span>
        </a>
        <a href={url('/lens/start-here')} class="first-card first-card-fallback">
          <div class="first-card-tag mono">OR</div>
          <h3>None of those, show me the full guide</h3>
          <p>The Start here page has a lookup table by situation. It also covers the four starting paths and how to install.</p>
          <span class="first-card-cue mono">FULL GUIDE →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE STACKS -->
  <section class="section section-alt dwell-pin" id="stacks">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={280} tiltX={50} tiltY={-15} spin={120} scrollSpin={-110} style="top: 8%; right: 5%;" enterFrom="right" />
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">004 · THE STACKS</div>
        <h2 class="reveal">The library has five stacks that keep growing.</h2>
        <p class="lead reveal">
          We've organised the library by what you're trying to ship rather
          than by tool, so you can pull what you need and ignore the rest.
        </p>
        <div class="lens-stacks stagger">
          <a href={url('/lens/brand')} class="lens-stack">
            <div class="stack-num mono">STACK · BRAND</div>
            <h3>Brand &amp; positioning</h3>
            <p>
              Start with a positioning audit or a naming sprint. The voice
              playbooks run from extraction through to a full message house.
            </p>
            <p class="stack-count mono">7 playbooks · growing →</p>
          </a>
          <a href={url('/lens/demand')} class="lens-stack">
            <div class="stack-num mono">STACK · DEMAND</div>
            <h3>Demand &amp; growth</h3>
            <p>
              Plan your channel mix and race-day demand here. Ambassador and
              sponsorship programmes live here too.
            </p>
            <p class="stack-count mono">11 playbooks · growing →</p>
          </a>
          <a href={url('/lens/content')} class="lens-stack">
            <div class="stack-num mono">STACK · CONTENT</div>
            <h3>Content &amp; channels</h3>
            <p>
              SEO clusters and eval-gated drafting are the core. News desks
              and earned-media pitches build on them.
            </p>
            <p class="stack-count mono">9 playbooks · growing →</p>
          </a>
          <a href={url('/lens/ops')} class="lens-stack">
            <div class="stack-num mono">STACK · OPS</div>
            <h3>Operating systems</h3>
            <p>
              Brief-to-ship pipelines keep the work moving. Brand guardrails
              written as code keep it on-brand.
            </p>
            <p class="stack-count mono">10 playbooks · growing →</p>
          </a>
          <a href={url('/lens/productivity')} class="lens-stack">
            <div class="stack-num mono">STACK · PRODUCTIVITY</div>
            <h3>Productivity &amp; back office</h3>
            <p>
              These workflows turn Cowork into a second brain, starting with
              daily briefings and email triage.
            </p>
            <p class="stack-count mono">10 playbooks · growing →</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ACCESS -->
  <section class="section section-alt dwell-pin" id="subscribe">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={300} tiltX={50} tiltY={-18} spin={130} scrollSpin={-100} style="top: 6%; right: -6%;" enterFrom="right" />
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">005 · FREE TO READ, SUBSCRIBE FOR UPDATES</div>
        <h2 class="reveal">It's free to read. You can <span class="gradient-text">subscribe</span> for what's new.</h2>
        <p class="lead reveal">
          You can read every playbook and every skill free, without signing
          up. The capability reference and AI-news pipeline are free too.
          Subscribe with your email if you want a heads-up when new entries
          ship and when we refresh existing ones against new frontier models.
        </p>
        <div class="lens-price reveal">
          <div class="lens-price-inner">
            <div class="price-head">
              <div class="price-tag mono"><span>FREE TO READ</span><span class="price-flag">EMAIL OPTIONAL</span></div>
              <div class="price-amount">£0<span class="price-per">/forever</span></div>
              <p class="price-shape mono">No paywall · Unsubscribe anytime</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="price-list">
              <li><strong>It's free without signing up.</strong> Read every playbook and every skill at <a href={url('/lens/library')}>/lens/library</a>, with nothing in the way.</li>
              <li><strong>It's free to install.</strong> The plugin is MIT-licensed and lives on GitHub. Add it in Cowork, or with two commands in Claude Code, to get all 28 skills.</li>
              <li><strong>Subscribe for the changes.</strong> We email you when new playbooks ship and when we refresh existing entries. There's also an optional weekly AI-news summary.</li>
              <li><strong>You get roughly one email a week.</strong> There's no upsell or drip funnel. You can unsubscribe in one click.</li>
            </ul>
            {/*
              Kit (ConvertKit) embedded-form endpoint. Form ID 9490842,
              UID cf656e168b. The form posts via fetch (handler in
              Footer.astro) and reads Kit's JSON status, so the user
              stays on the page and only sees success if Kit accepted it.

              Switching services later only needs the action URL and
              field name updated. Kit uses `email_address`, Mailchimp
              uses `EMAIL`, Buttondown uses `email`.
            */}
            <form
              class="lens-signup-form"
              data-newsletter-form
              action="https://app.kit.com/forms/9490842/subscriptions"
              method="POST"
              novalidate
            >
              <label for="lens-email-signup" class="sr-only">Email address</label>
              <input
                type="email"
                id="lens-email-signup"
                name="email_address"
                placeholder="your@email.com"
                required
                autocomplete="email"
              />
              <button type="submit" class="btn-cta" data-newsletter-submit>
                <span data-submit-label>Subscribe for updates</span>
              </button>
            </form>
            <p class="lens-signup-feedback" data-newsletter-feedback role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <p class="price-note">
              <a href={url('/privacy')}>What we do with your data</a>. You can also skip the email and read the library at <a href={url('/lens/library')}>/lens/library</a> any time.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE LENS PLUGIN -->
  <section class="section dwell-pin" id="plugin">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={300} tiltX={56} tiltY={-15} spin={140} scrollSpin={-80} style="top: 6%; right: 5%;" enterFrom="right" />
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">006 · THE LENS PLUGIN</div>
        <h2 class="reveal">Your AI agent runs 28 marketing skills <span class="gradient-text">inside Cowork</span>.</h2>
        <p class="lead reveal">
          The skills in the plugin do the work that the playbooks on this
          site explain. Add the plugin once from Cowork's plugin menu, then
          ask Claude to set up The Lens. The onboarding skill finds your
          brand documentation and builds a <code>.lens/</code> workspace
          around it. Then it recommends a starter. A working setup takes
          twenty to forty minutes. After that every skill below runs
          against your actual data.
        </p>
        <pre class="lens-skills-install reveal"><code>Customize → Plugins → Add marketplace
Scylark/manual-focus → install the-lens
set up the lens</code></pre>
        <p class="lens-skills-note reveal">
          In Claude Code, run <code>/plugin marketplace add Scylark/manual-focus</code>, then <code>/plugin install the-lens@manual-focus</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="lens-skills-cta reveal">
          <a href={url('/lens/skills')} class="btn-cta">Browse the skills</a>
          <a href={url('/lens/cowork')} class="btn-ghost">Read the Cowork primer</a>
        </div>
        <p class="lens-skills-note reveal">
          28 skills live · 26 workflow skills · 1 onboarding orchestrator · 1 video-render utility · Source on <a href="https://github.com/Scylark/manual-focus/tree/master/lens-skills" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHO IT'S FOR -->
  <section class="section section-alt dwell-pin">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={320} tiltX={55} tiltY={20} spin={-160} scrollSpin={80} style="top: 6%; right: 4%;" enterFrom="right" />
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">007 · WHO IT'S FOR</div>
        <h2 class="reveal">We built it for senior operators.</h2>
        <div class="lens-fit-grid">
          <div class="lens-fit reveal">
            <h3>Built for</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Heads of marketing and CMOs at £5M–£150M brands, especially in endurance and sports</li>
              <li>Fractional CMOs running two to four portfolio clients</li>
              <li>Senior in-house operators who own brand or growth</li>
              <li>Marketing leaders at AI-native startups who want depth over hot takes</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="lens-fit reveal">
            <h3>Look elsewhere if you're</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>A generalist trying to break into marketing</li>
              <li>An agency looking to resell the workflows as your own</li>
              <li>Hoping for a "five prompts to grow your business" listicle</li>
              <li>Planning to skim rather than ship</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHO CURATES IT -->
  <section class="section dwell-pin">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={400} tiltX={58} tiltY={-18} spin={160} scrollSpin={100} style="top: 6%; right: 4%;" enterFrom="right" />
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">008 · WHO CURATES IT</div>
        <h2 class="big-statement reveal" data-scroll-scale style="transform-origin: left center;">
          Operators who<br/>
          <span class="gradient-text">run the work</span><br/>
          curate it.
        </h2>
        <p class="lead reveal">
          Manual Focus curates The Lens, with a rotating cast of
          contributors from the Foundry collective. We're a marketing
          agency for endurance and sports brands, run by senior operators.
          The playbooks hold the method our work produced. They include the
          prompts and eval gates we use. They also name the failure modes
          we've watched go wrong over the years.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal">
          As engagements run and patterns prove themselves, we replace the
          illustrative examples in each entry with real ones. The eval
          shapes get updated with what those runs produced. When we retire a
          workflow, the entry says so and explains why. When a frontier
          model changes a workflow's result, we annotate the affected
          entries.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="section dwell-pin">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={260} tiltX={55} tiltY={-22} spin={140} scrollSpin={70} style="top: 8%; left: 4%;" enterFrom="left" />
      <div class="container">
        <div class="eyebrow">009 · BEFORE YOU GO IN</div>
        <h2 class="reveal">You'd be right to ask these questions.</h2>
        <div class="lens-faq stagger">
          <details class="lens-faq-item">
            <summary>It's really free?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes. Every playbook and every skill is free, with no paywall
              and no card details. The capability reference and AI-news
              pipeline are free too. We ask for your email so we can tell
              you when new entries ship, but the library is open at
              <a href={url('/lens/library')}>/lens/library</a> without
              signing up.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="lens-faq-item">
            <summary>What's in it for Manual Focus, then?</summary>
            <p>
              The Lens is how people get to know us. Senior marketers who
              use the playbooks sometimes find work that fits a
              <a href={url('/services/')}>Manual Focus engagement</a>. A free,
              opinionated library that we keep updating is how we earn that
              conversation. If you never need us, that's fine too.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="lens-faq-item">
            <summary>How is this different from a course?</summary>
            <p>
              You work through a course once, but you keep coming back to
              The Lens as a reference. Pull a playbook the day a brief lands.
              Swap the model when a new one ships. Hand a workflow to a junior
              with the eval harness intact. It's closer to a Bloomberg
              Terminal than a Udemy unit.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="lens-faq-item">
            <summary>How many playbooks are in there now?</summary>
            <p>
              There are 47 live across five stacks. There are also 28
              skills you can install as a Cowork and Claude Code plugin.
              Twenty-six of them are workflow skills. The other two are the
              setup-the-lens onboarding skill plus a utility that turns
              playbooks into avatar videos through the HeyGen API. The
              capability reference page grades what AI can do this quarter.
              We add new entries as patterns prove themselves in live work.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="lens-faq-item">
            <summary>Can I share with my team?</summary>
            <p>
              Yes. Pass the links around and install the plugin in every
              team member's Cowork, because we built the library for
              working teams to use.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="lens-faq-item">
            <summary>What if a model change breaks a workflow I'm running?</summary>
            <p>
              When a frontier model lands, we re-test the affected entries.
              We note what changed and which prompts we updated. We also say
              whether the workflow still ships in the same shape. If your
              version is running fine, you don't need to touch it.
              Subscribers hear from us when we refresh an entry they'd care
              about.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details class="lens-faq-item">
            <summary>Is this a replacement for hiring Manual Focus?</summary>
            <p>
              For teams that can run the playbooks themselves, yes, it gives
              you the method without the cost of a Fractional CMO. Other
              teams use it alongside one of <a href={url('/services/')}>the
              services</a> to keep the in-house team sharp between
              engagements.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CLOSE -->
  <section class="section cta-close dwell-pin">
    <div class="dwell-pin-stage">
      <FocusObject size={520} tiltX={60} tiltY={-20} spin={160} scrollSpin={100} style="top: -10%; left: -10%;" enterFrom="left" />
      <FocusObject size={360} tiltX={50} tiltY={25} spin={-130} scrollSpin={-90} style="bottom: -10%; right: -8%;" enterFrom="right" />

      <div class="container cta-close-inner">
        <h2 class="cta-headline reveal">
          Read the work, or<br/>
          <span class="gradient-text">pick one playbook and ship it.</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="cta-sub reveal">
          You get the most from The Lens by running it. Start with the
          guide if you're new, or go straight to the library if you know
          what you're after.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-close-buttons reveal">
          <a href={url('/lens/start-here')} class="btn-cta">Start here</a>
          <a href={url('/lens/library')} class="btn-ghost">Browse the library</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ============================
     LENS HERO
     ============================ */
  /* Hero shares the same container width as the rest of the
